+# Q3 revenue drop: East
+
+East had the biggest percentage fall in revenue from Q2 to Q3 of any region: down 29.79%, from $333,747.57 to $234,325.08 (−$99,422.49). Ledger Pro accounts for most of it. Its East revenue went from $106,520.77 to $23,015.24, a fall of $83,505.53, which is about 84% of the region's drop. This was lost volume, not lower prices: completed Ledger Pro orders in East fell from about 100 a month to 22–28 a month in July–September, while the average price stayed near $49. Volume came back in October. Revenue here is units × unit_price over completed rows only, with refunds (negative units) included. The data has rows dated up to 31 December, so Q4 includes dates that are still in the future.
+
+| Quarter | East revenue | Change vs previous quarter |
+|---------|-------------:|---------------------------:|
+| Q1      |  $333,565.48 |                          — |
+| Q2      |  $333,747.57 |                     +0.05% |
+| Q3      |  $234,325.08 |                    −29.79% |
+| Q4      |  $305,168.76 |                    +30.23% |
